WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.391
The X-Men are not currently part of the Marvel
Cinematic Universe, but if they were, the

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.940
only X-Man to survive the Snap would've spelled
big trouble for Thanos.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:12.740
Speaking with IGN's Up at Noon show, Avengers:
Endgame directors Joe and Anthony Russo revealed

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:16.309
the one member of the team they would have
left standing, and they have some pretty solid

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:17.500
reasoning behind their choice.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:21.520
The Russos' conversation with IGN involved
a thought experiment in which the pair were

00:00:21.529 --> 00:00:25.770
asked about several groups of people, some
fictional and some not, and which members

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.400
would have survived what Marvel refers to
as the "Decimation."

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.080
When it came to the X-Men, they didn't hesitate
to assert that only one mutant would have

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:33.350
made it: Wolverine.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:36.640
Upon being handed a picture of some popular
X-Men, Joe Russo said:

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.160
"This is going to be interesting.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.920
I'm going to do something very controversial."

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.480
To the surprise of the hosts and encouragement
from his brother, Joe began striking team

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.410
members willy-nilly, taking the time to point
out that even through Thanos wiped out half

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:54.480
of all life in the universe, it doesn't necessarily
mean that every specific group of people would

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:54.980
have been halved.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.700
"Hawkeye's entire family disappeared.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:02.120
So any given group, you could lose almost
everyone in that group."

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:05.880
Russo then presented his handiwork to gasps
from the hosts.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.000
He explained the thought process behind his
choice:

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:09.660
"I'd love to see a--" "I don't want to give
you the rest of these cards."

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:14.520
"--fiercely motivated Wolverine going up against
Thanos."

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:19.280
It stands to reason that nothing would motivate
the near-indestructible hero quite like the

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:23.480
only family he knows being wantonly wiped
out by a genocidal intergalactic warlord.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:24.940
It would have been quite a contest.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:29.280
We know that Thanos' mighty sword is capable
of damaging vibranium, given what it did to

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.280
Captain America's shield.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.820
But we haven't seen Thanos go up against adamantium,
the metal that makes up Wolverine's claws

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:38.680
and covers his skeleton, in the MCU yet, though
it has happened in comics.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:43.430
After that difficult choice, the Russos were
then presented with a series of similar scenarios,

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:47.149
revealing in each instance which members of
popular groups they would have chosen to dust.

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:51.329
For the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles, Joe
Russo claimed to own a copy of the very first

00:01:51.329 --> 00:01:53.770
issue of the comic, saying "I love these guys."

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:55.400
But that doesn't mean he would have spared
them all.

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:59.520
The choice was so tough he deferred to Anthony,
who benevolently spared them all.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.900
Lest the hosts think him soft, though, Anthony
deadpanned:

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:06.300
"Remember, you're talking to the guys who
iced Spider-Man and Black Panther."

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.450
Next up was Scooby-Doo and the gang.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:13.320
Fred, whom Joe called "kind of worthless,"
and Shaggy both bit the dust, presumably leaving

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:16.730
Scooby, Velma and Daphne with unstoppable
thirsts for vengeance.

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:19.900
After that, the duo was handed a photo of
the cast of Friends.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:24.020
As the Russos mused about the slim likelihood
of an entire group having the misfortune of

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:27.210
being totally wiped out, Anthony marked an
X over every face.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:30.720
At least Ross wouldn't have to pine over a
dusted Rachel for five years.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.560
After briefly misidentifying a Member of the
Backstreet Boys as New Kids on the Block's

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:39.100
Donnie Wahlberg, the directing brothers decided
to leave only one standing: Nick Carter.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:42.540
They didn't seem to have any particular reason
for this; Nick just got lucky.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:43.600
It's all random, anyway.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:44.900
"I offered a solution."

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:47.080
"Genocide."

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:49.120
"But random.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:50.360
Dispassionate.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.360
Fair to rich and poor alike."

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:56.660
Having earned the attention of Marvel Studios
partly due to their excellent work on the

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:00.490
beloved series Arrested Development, deciding
which Bluths to wipe out had to have been

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.040
a tough choice for the Russos to make.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:07.080
Maeby, Buster, and Tobias all bite the dust,
with Anthony explaining that Tobias had to

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.490
go because he thought it would be funny to
hear the blue man's final words, with David

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.700
Cross doing "40 variations" on the line.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:16.200
"Oh my God, we're having a fire!

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:17.580
Sale!

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.960
Oh the burning!

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.860
It burns me!"

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.540
For the cast of another comedy the brothers
worked on, Community, Pierce Hawthorne got

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:29.000
dusted, with Anthony noting that he, quote,
"could use the five years."

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:33.310
Joe then mused over what choices would be
heartbreaking narratively before finally choosing

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:34.690
to spare everyone else.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:38.810
Disney's deal to acquire Fox didn't go through
soon enough for an epic throwdown between

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:43.370
Wolverine and Thanos to become a reality,
but Logan will surely be a part of the MCU

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:44.700
at some point in the future.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:48.360
If Thanos ever manages to return, viewers
might get to see them go head-to-head, and

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.060
Wolverine has gotten the better of the Titan
once or twice in the comics.

